Subject: [PATCH 233/234] Patch 0233: a field battle starts the moment it is
 triggered (MOD_OPT_QUICK_BATTLE). No BATTLE letters: the tamer's walk back is
 run unseen at once and the Digimon that do not join leave at once; no flee
 bubbles. BTL_REL is read ahead in the world at its own address (checksum over
 btl_START..btl_END, blocked for the screen by any other overlay: fishing,
 curling, menus, evolution, shops) and the fight starts on it; the music font
 (read asynchronously), the battle's sound bank, the enemies' voices, then the
 EFE engine and the techniques' effects load while it runs, in the original's
 staging order at GENERAL_BUFFER, the file queue stepped at every vblank wait
 (MOD_LOAD_PUMP). No technique starts and no item menu opens before the
 effects are in; what is still loading lands before the fight's clean-up. 2
 780 bytes of heap

